  "title": "Amazon Pivots Cloud Gaming Strategy and Faces Antitrust and MMO Ties",
  "summary": "Amazon is pivoting its cloud gaming strategy by introducing Luna to Prime Video and testing ad-supported streaming, while also severing ties with two other MMOs (Lost Ark and Throne) and facing antitrust lawsuits in New Jersey and New York. The company has also announced plans to train on Twitch streamers’ content by default.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Amazon is introducing Luna to Prime Video to target different players.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Amazon is handing over live operations of Throne and Liberty and Lost Ark to other companies.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "New Jersey sues Amazon on antitrust grounds, accusing it of unlawfully wielding power over delivery contractors.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
